+Do not replace Android 16 `NfcNci.apk` with the Android 15 Exynos9810 package:
+it does not implement the Android 16 `INfcAdapter` interface. The M4 branch
+keeps the donor Android 17 APEX instead of looking for that Android 16 path.
+Static ELF inspection shows the APEX JNI references HIDL NFC 1.0/1.2 and AIDL;
+the target HAL provides HIDL 1.0/1.1/1.2. The separate BZI6 `SecNfc.apk` is
+version17 and references both HIDL and AIDL `ISehNfc`, while the selected S9+
+service exposes Samsung HIDL 2.0 only. This leaves vendor-manager/UI path
+selection to runtime verification. Validate service startup, tag discovery/read,
+and Samsung NFC UI from device logs before claiming support. The Android 15 SEC
+JNI is also incompatible with Android 16's `NativeNfcManager`.
 
 The shared HAL files live under `common/vendor`. Device-specific S3NRN82
 firmware and RF calibration files live under each target directory.
